The argument is one empty string, which names no subcommand, so it is refused
the same way any other unknown word is.

This is as close as the harness can come to `md` with no arguments at all.
run.py raises on an empty `args` file, so an empty argument LIST cannot be
staged, and the zero-argument behaviour - printing the root help and exiting 0 -
is not covered by this suite. cli-help-prints-the-overview-to-stdout pins the
same help text through `md --help`.

stderr is not pinned. ArgumentParser answers a refusal with md's own sentence
followed by the whole usage line for the command, and that usage line names
every option the command has. Pinning it would turn "someone added a flag" into
a failure of this case, which guards the exit status instead. md's own stderr,
with no usage line around it, is pinned in the two
list-fails-when-... cases.
